<title>SWITZERLAND: ABB wins Taiwan contract.</title>
<headline>ABB wins Taiwan contract.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>ABB Kraftwerke AG, a unit of Swiss-Swedish engineering group ABB Asea Brown Boveri, said it had won an order worth more than $160 million to expand a power plant in Taiwan.</p>
<p>The order will increase total output which involves the gas-fired Tung Hsiao power plant to approximately 1,700 megawatts from 320 megawatts. The project is due for completion by July 2000.</p>
<p>ABB will supply two type GT11N2 gas turbines as well as heat recovery steam generators, one steam turbine, electricity generators, the overall power plant control system and the balance of plant equipment. ABB will also provide engineering and installation.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
